error: rsjs boundary: `rsjs::server_attr(...)` cannot declare or read `signal(...)`

       Why:
         Server-only attributes are static SSR values, not reactive client state.

       Use one of:
         - Declare state before the template and use a normal dynamic attribute for reactive values.
         - Use `rsjs::server_attr(...)` only for values that are intentionally static after hydration.

       Tracked feature:
         server_boundary.state_declaration
  --> tests/ui/conformance/fail/39_server_attr_state_declaration.rs:16:46
   |
16 |             <button class={rsjs::server_attr(signal("active").get())}>"Save"</button>
   |                                              ^^^^^^
